# TODO - EDMA/interrupts

## Objective

Implement ring allocation, IOMMU/DMA contracts, RX/TX ownership, descriptors,
completion, interrupt handling, memory safety, sleep and fault recovery in
source. Consult public ath9k and IOKit documentation. **No physical packet
transfer required.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Bound DMA ownership, interrupts, completion and power-off quiescence.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Allocate/map actual descriptor, status-ring and packet buffers through
      the provider's IOMMU/DMA contracts. Bound alignment, lengths, 32-bit
      device addresses and segment coverage; specify coherency/directions.
- [ ] Program RX/TX queues and doorbells, decode real completions and deliver
      actual received buffers. Metadata-only reservations are incomplete.
- [ ] Implement interrupt source/work-loop setup, masking/acknowledgement,
      deferred work and teardown, with no blocking hard-interrupt operation.
- [ ] Define publish/retire ownership, barriers and nonreused generations for
      every ring/buffer. Handle stale completions, overflow/underrun, queue
      pressure and reset without double free, reuse or unbounded waits.
- [ ] Quiesce producers/interrupts/device DMA before releasing mappings on
      failure, stop and sleep. Quarantine uncertain ownership; implement the
      real cleanup/recovery path and fresh resume generations.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
